WEBVTT

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:30.746
and write papers in their home institutes.

00:02:31.413 --> 00:02:34.621
Then, they wanted to share their findings
with all their colleagues.

00:02:34.663 --> 00:02:36.746
To make this information sharing easy,

00:02:36.788 --> 00:02:40.121
we created the web in the early 1990′s.

00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:43.371
Physicists no longer needed to know
where the information was stored

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:45.621
in order to find it
and access it on the web,

00:02:45.663 --> 00:02:47.663
an idea which caught on across the world

00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:50.704
and has transformed the way
we communicate in our daily lives.

00:02:52.413 --> 00:02:56.038
During the early 2000′s,
the continued growth of our big data

00:02:56.079 --> 00:02:58.913
outstripped our capability
to analyse it at CERN,

00:02:58.954 --> 00:03:01.871
despite having buildings
full of computers.